# Files that start a process themselves (tools/check-process-starts.py, docs/PROCESSES.md):
# <path> <count of lines found> <reason>

# The two helpers.
crates/appkit-core/src/child.rs 2 the helper for children of the app
crates/appkit-hub/src/launch.rs 2 the helper for a program of somebody else (it outlives the hub on purpose)

# Named exceptions that stay (decided 2026-11-14): Neovim as the editor in a visible console of its own, a window the person asked for and works in; a link handed to the system (ShellExecuteW) starts no process of the app.
crates/appkit-hub/src/browser.rs 2 hands a link to the default browser (ShellExecuteW; open and xdg-open go through launch)
crates/appkit-hub/src/editor.rs 5 named exception: Neovim in a visible console; the file manager and the folder dialog move (tasks of their own)

# Named exception that stays: the hub puts itself in the background (a case of its own, not a child of an app). Its calls of reg.exe, taskkill.exe and kill are system tools that are replaced by tasks of their own.
crates/appkit-hub/src/background.rs 5 named exception: the hub in the background; reg.exe, taskkill.exe, kill are replaced later
crates/appkit-core/src/registry.rs 1 icacls.exe on the secret file, a blocking call that has not moved to the helper yet

# A test program (it plays a child that starts a process of its own).
crates/appkit-testkit/src/bin/child-probe.rs 2 the probe of the child tests (a grandchild, and the control start of a hub without a console)
